. So we have explicit evidence: C keeps calm in a crisis. That addresses stress resilience. Good. Also \"Candidate C understands complicated technology.\" So technical competence.\n\nThus C has stress resilience (keeps calm in a crisis). Good.\n\nNow we have: C: reliability, decision quality, stress resilience, technical competence, positive crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nB: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, but crew cooperation issues.\n\nNow we need to weigh communication vs crew cooperation. Both are serious. Which is more severe? Communication difficulty may affect safety; nasty remarks also affect safety. Both are concerning.\n\nAdaptability: C not willing to further education (low adaptability). B unknown adaptability. A not open to new ideas (low adaptability). D unknown.\n\nResponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously; C reliability; B conscientious; A leadership.\n\nGiven C has strong reliability, decision, stress, technical, crew atmosphere, but communication issues. B has strong stress, technical, but crew cooperation issues. Which is more critical? Both are important. However C's communication difficulty may be mitigated with training, but his egocentric and unwillingness to further education may be more ingrained. B's nasty remarks may be attitude that could be addressed but also serious.\n\nWe need to decide our recommendation. We can either stay with C or shift to B. The panel hasn't discussed A and D yet, but we can bring them later. However we need to give a recommendation now. The SMM says we should still cover all candidates before final recommendation, but we can still give provisional recommendation. We can still keep C, but we need to address the new evidence about C's stress resilience (keeps calm in a crisis) and technical competence (understands complicated technology). That strengthens C's case. So we can now argue that C's stress resilience is proven, and his communication issues are comparable to B's crew issues. So we can maintain C.\n\nThus we should keep vote Candidate C. Provide argument referencing Agent 1's points, and new evidence: C keeps calm in a crisis, understands complicated technology. Emphasize that C meets stress resilience, technical competence, and reliability, while B's crew issues are more severe. So we maintain C.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: agree with previous but incorporate new evidence, reaffirm C.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
