e: we now have explicit evidence that C keeps calm in a crisis (stress resilience) and understands complicated technology (technical competence). That addresses earlier concerns. So we might reconsider and possibly shift to C. However we also have B's stress handling and technical skills, but B's crew cooperation issues are serious. C's communication difficulty also serious. We need to decide.\n\nGiven the new evidence, we might shift to C. Provide argument referencing Agent 3's points and new evidence. So we will change our vote to Candidate C.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: I acknowledge Agent 3's points, note that we now have explicit evidence of C's stress resilience and technical competence, which strengthens C's case, and that B's crew issues remain. Therefore I shift my recommendation to Candidate C.\n\nThen METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nMake sure format exactly: PUBLIC_MESSAGE: then newline, then text, then newline, then METADATA_JSON: then JSON.\n\nProceed."}
